OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGITC RECEIVES TELETEXT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGFRANCHISE BIDS
OL,5, Five bids have been received by the
OL,6, Independent Television Commission to
OL,7, run the ITV and Channel Four teletext
OL,8, service from 1993.
OL,10,FAs in the television franchise
OL,11,Fprocedure, the highest bidder must also
OL,12,Fconvince the ITC it can finance the
OL,13,F10-year licence as well as pass a
OL,14,F"quality threshold" on planned content.
OL,16,FOracle, the existing franchise-holder,
OL,17,Fhas applied to keep its licence. Other
OL,18,Fbids have come from groups backed by
OL,19,Fcompanies such as TV-am, Associated
OL,20,FNewspapers, Carlton Communications and
OL,21,FITN.
OL,23,D]FFromG20-01-92F/Gteletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFNat Radio
